# Mocking API Calls

To test components that fetch data, use **MSW (Mock Service Worker)** to intercept network requests.

```js
import { rest } from 'msw';
import { setupServer } from 'msw/node';

const server = setupServer(
  rest.get('/api/posts', (req, res, ctx) => {
    return res(ctx.json([{ id: 1, title: 'Test' }]));
  })
);
```

This avoids real HTTP calls and gives you full control over responses.

slides.codeSnippet:
// __tests__/PostsPage.test.js
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import { rest } from 'msw';
import { setupServer } from 'msw/node';
import PostsPage from '../app/posts/page';

const server = setupServer(
  rest.get('https://api.example.com/posts', (req, res, ctx) =>
    res(ctx.json([{ id: 1, title: 'Hello World' }]))
  )
);

beforeAll(() => server.listen());
afterEach(() => server.resetHandlers());
afterAll(() => server.close());

describe('PostsPage', () => {
  it('renders posts', async () => {
    render(await PostsPage()); // Server Component: call directly
    expect(screen.getByText('Hello World')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
